---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Local API Usage Cost Checker — AICost Matrix" description="Check complete direct Anthropic Messages JSON records locally. See cache billing buckets, flag duplicates and export a token-fee calculation." canonical="https://aicost.apexcraftweb.com/usage">
<div class="wrap narrow flow"><section><p class="eyebrow">Inspect the billing inputs</p><h1>Explain a usage record.</h1><p class="intro" style="color:#606b80">Map a small set of direct Claude API responses to token fees. No API key or account needed.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Complete responses, one price basis</h2><p>Supports Claude Sonnet 5.5, Haiku 5.5 and Opus 5.5 direct Messages JSON. Paste one response, a JSON array, or one complete response per line (JSONL). Maximum 500 records / 1 MB. Remove prompts, output content, customer identifiers and keys first.</p><p class="hint">Not for streaming fragments, SDK-normalized traces, Bedrock, Vertex, other providers or historical invoice verification. Input tokens in this API exclude cache reads and writes. Cache writes require the explicit 5m/1h breakdown.</p>
<label for="usageMode">Billing mode for every pasted response<select id="usageMode"><option value="standard">Standard · global</option><option value="batch">Message Batches · global</option></select></label>
<label for="usageRecords">Redacted complete response JSON / JSONL<textarea id="usageRecords" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" placeholder='{"id":"msg_example","type":"message","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","usage":{"input_tokens":1000,"output_tokens":500}}'></textarea></label>
<label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="confirmScope"/><span>I confirm these are direct Claude API text-only calls with global routing, no server tools or fast/priority mode, using the selected billing mode. I want an estimate at the stored reference prices, not a historical bill.</span></label>
<div class="actions"><button class="primary" id="inspectUsage" type="button">Check records</button><button class="secondary" id="loadUsageExample" type="button">Load fictional example</button><button class="secondary" id="clearUsage" type="button">Clear records</button></div>
<p class="hint">Parsing runs in this page. Raw responses are not sent by this tool, saved in browser storage or included in exports. Normalized token counts are included in calculation exports. Opening the website still creates normal hosting/network requests; see <a href="/privacy">privacy details</a>.</p>
<p class="error" id="usageError" role="alert" hidden></p>
<div id="usageOutput" hidden aria-live="polite"><h3>Estimated text token fees: <span id="usageTotal"></span></h3><p id="usageSummary"></p><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Normalized billing buckets · per response</caption><thead><tr><th>Row / model</th><th>Uncached</th><th>Cache read</th><th>Write 5m</th><th>Write 1h</th><th>Output</th><th>USD estimate</th></tr></thead><tbody id="usageRows"></tbody></table></div>
<p class="hint">Prices checked 2026-11-14. This is a formula estimate, not a provider-reported charge. Export includes token counts and calculations, but excludes original message IDs and raw content.</p><button class="primary" id="downloadUsage" type="button">Download calculation</button></div>
<noscript><p>JavaScript is required to inspect records locally.</p></noscript></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Still different from the provider bill?</h2><ol><li>Match the same billing period, currency, project and provider channel. Check whether the dashboard has finished updating.</li><li>Confirm exact model IDs, billed mode, regional premiums, credits, discounts and tax.</li><li>Count every paid retry or fallback once. Do not combine streaming snapshots as separate complete responses.</li><li>Keep uncached input, cache reads and both cache write durations separate. Do not add thinking tokens to output twice.</li><li>Check tool/media charges and infrastructure outside this tool. Missing records cannot be recovered from a price table.</li></ol><p>We do not compute an invoice error percentage from unmatched totals. Use the calculation export to trace the inputs, then compare like for like.</p><a href="/methodology">Supported schema and price sources →</a></section></div>
</Layout>
<script>
import '../scripts/usage';
</script>
